   :title "deal-tells-on-commit-not-on-friend-sync"
   :text "RESULT: deal-tells-on-commit-not-on-friend-sync sha=<sha12> tier: frontier REPO: mas-bandwidth/nova-sprint BASE: v1.3/comms STOP: a card dealt to a friend row (the coordinator seat's own included) is delivered to its inbox and told on the bus within one log event of the tick that commits the deal, not at the next friend sync --every pass; the seat's own row is told as kind=status; --every stays as the quiet-log backs Source: Glenn 13:57Z 2026-10-15: \"Event driven push notifications are vastly superior to polling. What else is like this? A poll where it should be a push notification to you, across nova tools and nova sprint?\"; the push audit of that hour (nova-tools abd4a6d, nova-sprint 3e51974), item 4 (and the friend-sync hop of 6). Work audited 2026-10-15. Pushed heads: 254ca3129cfa068d5db7a1ca1fda7eb672c4c71f (emma; on origin: sprint/deal-tells-on-commit-not-on-friend-sync.w1.g1.e21, sprint/deal-tells-on-commit-not-on-friend-sync.w2.g4.e21, sprint/deal-tells-on-commit-not-on-friend-sync.w3.g1.e21); 2b7e0652bd6e85419fa23ad1b026a641f5285eec (stella; on origin: sprint/deal-tells-on-commit-not-on-friend-sync.w2.g4.e21, sprint/deal-tells-on-commit-not-on-friend-sync.w3.g1.e21). Working branch, not on origin: sprint/deal-tells-on-commit-not-on-friend-sync.w3.g3.e21 (emma, working when dropped). "
