  (item "a-red-base-gets-its-fix-red-worked" :group "export-v13-blockers" :area "nova-sprint"
   :title "a-red-base-gets-its-fix-red-worked"
   :text "RESULT: a-red-base-gets-its-fix-red-worked sha=<sha12> tier: frontier REPO: mas-bandwidth/nova-sprint BASE: v1.3/comms STOP: when a base fails its tree gate on a class (gofmt, vet, class-tests), the fix-red card the generator names is admitted to that base's stream at once with PRIORITY blocker and first in line, dealt by the next tick with no coordinator step, and its landing closes the base-red episode and resumes  Source: Glenn 14:35Z 2026-10-15: \"I like this approach. I am happy to run you at Medium or High for important things. If you could run some things at low that would be great.\" (the sprint must be smooth enough to coordinate at low effort; this gap forced hand-work the same day). Work audited 2026-10-15. Pushed heads: 627ada6eb8c9b6a92a7092d1ba1467e35bbe1725 (rowan; on origin: sprint/a-red-base-gets-its-fix-red-worked.w1.g1.e21, sprint/a-red-base-gets-its-fix-red-worked.w2.g1.e21); c751741a3a3b7587be64a7008ae0872afbde4679 (rowan; on origin: sprint/a-red-base-gets-its-fix-red-worked.w2.g1.e21). Working branch, not on origin: sprint/a-red-base-gets-its-fix-red-worked.w3.g1.e21 (emma, working when dropped). "
