  (item "finish-auto-take-hands-the-card-to-a-worker" :group "export-v13-blockers" :area "nova-sprint"
   :title "finish-auto-take-hands-the-card-to-a-worker"
   :text "RESULT: finish-auto-take-hands-the-card-to-a-worker sha=<sha12> tier: frontier REPO: mas-bandwidth/nova-sprint BASE: v1.3/comms STOP: a friend's finish never leaves a card in working with no worker on it: the next ready card it takes is handed to that friend's worker launcher by one bus push in the same commit (or not taken at all when the friend has no launcher that answers), a taken card no longer flaps back to rea Source: Glenn 14:35Z 2026-10-15: \"I like this approach. I am happy to run you at Medium or High for important things. If you could run some things at low that would be great.\" (the sprint must be smooth enough to coordinate at low effort; this gap forced hand-work the same day). Work audited 2026-10-15. No pushed head. Working branch, not on origin: sprint/finish-auto-take-hands-the-card-to-a-worker.w3.g3.e21 (emma, working when dropped). "
   :why "Scoped out of the sprint by Glenn 2026-10-15: only the four tiny fixes stay in v13-blockers, tool-review-2026-10-15 and nova-local; the rest waits on the roadmap."
