  (item "deal-matches-published-gate-facts" :group "export-v13-blockers" :area "nova-sprint"
   :title "deal-matches-published-gate-facts"
   :text "RESULT: deal-matches-published-gate-facts sha=<sha12> tier: frontier REPO: mas-bandwidth/nova-sprint BASE: v1.3/comms STOP: `nova-sprint fleet beat <m> --facts <list>` stores the member's facts on its control card (FieldFacts), and every path that puts a work card on a unit (the machine deal, the friend deal, the rebalance and any redeal) gives a GATE-NEEDS card only to a unit whose facts cover every need; a card no  Source: Glenn 13:51Z 2026-10-15: \"Please card all the optimizations for architectures.\" The misdeal of 2026-10-15 (sprint epoch 21, `nova-sprint log --card spike-fixed-batch-neon-on-m5`): at 10:54 the machine deal held the card's GATE-NEEDS (darwin, arm64, sme2) and raised NGateNeeds (\"batman (facts: ); hetzner2 (facts: ); space (facts: ); superman (facts: )\"); at 11:02 attempt 1 was dealt to a friend seat anyway, and at 11:28 the rebalance moved it from that seat to b3 (\"its excess; a free lane takes i Work audited 2026-10-15. No pushed head. "
   :why "Scoped out of the sprint by Glenn 2026-10-15: only the four tiny fixes stay in v13-blockers, tool-review-2026-10-15 and nova-local; the rest waits on the roadmap."
   :date "2026-10-15"
   :origin "sprint card deal-matches-published-gate-facts (stream v13-blockers, column waiting, tier , base v1.3/comms), moved out of the sprint 2026-10-15"
   :kept (:sprint-card "deal-matches-published-gate-facts" :sprint-stream "v13-blockers" :sprint-column "waiting" :tier "" :sprint-base "v1.3/comms" :needs "members-publish-their-gate-facts" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch ""))
  (item "routes-rest-and-limit-resolve-every-listed-route" :group "export-v13-blockers" :area "nova-sprint"
   :title "routes-rest-and-limit-resolve-every-listed-route"
   :text "RESULT: routes-rest-and-limit-resolve-every-listed-route sha=<sha12> tier: frontier CARRY: routes-rest-and-limit-resolve-every-listed-route attempt 1 head=da363ca7fe02dab1f89fb400195fa18a144288c5 REPO: mas-bandwidth/nova-sprint BASE: v1.3/comms STOP: every route name `nova-sprint routes` prints (a ROUTE line) is resolved by `routes rest`, `routes wake` and `routes limit`, with and without --dry-run, on the mem twin a Source: the coordinator, epoch 21 (2026-10-15): `routes rest` and `routes limit` refused a route `routes` lists, verbatim: `REFUSED pro-glm53-openrouter: pro-glm53-openrouter names no route and no provider of a route (nova sprint routes lists them)`; the same day `nova-config route set --enabled false` reached the sprint only after a separate `nova-config apply --kind route`. Work audited 2026-10-15. Pushed heads: da363ca7fe02dab1f89fb400195fa18a144288c5 (emma; on origin: sprint/routes-rest-and-limit-resolve-every-listed-route.w1.g3.e21). "
   :why "Scoped out of the sprint by Glenn 2026-10-15: only the four tiny fixes stay in v13-blockers, tool-review-2026-10-15 and nova-local; the rest waits on the roadmap."
   :date "2026-10-15"
   :origin "sprint card routes-rest-and-limit-resolve-every-listed-route (stream v13-blockers, column ready, tier , base v1.3/comms), moved out of the sprint 2026-10-15"
   :kept (:sprint-card "routes-rest-and-limit-resolve-every-listed-route" :sprint-stream "v13-blockers" :sprint-column "ready" :tier "" :sprint-base "v1.3/comms" :needs "" :pushed-head "da363ca7fe02dab1f89fb400195fa18a144288c5" :pushed-branch "sprint/routes-rest-and-limit-resolve-every-listed-route.w1.g3.e21"))
  (item "a-released-pin-goes-only-to-another-friend" :group "export-v13-blockers" :area "nova-sprint"
   :title "a-released-pin-goes-only-to-another-friend"
   :text "RESULT: a-released-pin-goes-only-to-another-friend sha=<sha12> tier: frontier REPO: mas-bandwidth/nova-sprint BASE: v1.3/comms STOP: a work card whose brief says WHO: only friend <name> (OnlyFriend) still waits for that friend and is still released at its deadline (the existing 10-minute timed release, PinReleased in stops.go); once released it is placed by no path (the machine deal, the rebalance, the redeal, the me Source: the coordinator, epoch 21 (2026-10-15): hard-pinned cards tr15-table-r5, tr15-table-r3 and tr15-fuse-r1 were released at their 10-minute deadline and then dealt to fleet members, and the judgment \"a pinned card was dealt away from its friend\" recurred over 13 cards (j17228). The owner ruled 2026-10-15 about 16:36Z: keep the 10-minute pin release; a released pin goes only to another friend, never a fleet machine. Work audited 2026-10-15. No pushed head. Working branch, not on origin: sprint/a-released-pin-goes-only-to-another-friend.w1.g4.e21 (emma, working when dropped). "
   :why "Scoped out of the sprint by Glenn 2026-10-15: only the four tiny fixes stay in v13-blockers, tool-review-2026-10-15 and nova-local; the rest waits on the roadmap."
   :date "2026-10-15"
   :origin "sprint card a-released-pin-goes-only-to-another-friend (stream v13-blockers, column working, tier , base v1.3/comms), moved out of the sprint 2026-10-15"
   :kept (:sprint-card "a-released-pin-goes-only-to-another-friend" :sprint-stream "v13-blockers" :sprint-column "working" :tier "" :sprint-base "v1.3/comms" :needs "" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch ""))
  (item "check-warns-when-the-sprint-runs-serial" :group "export-v13-blockers" :area "nova-sprint"
   :title "check-warns-when-the-sprint-runs-serial"
   :text "RESULT: check-warns-when-the-sprint-runs-serial sha=<sha12> tier: frontier REPO: mas-bandwidth/nova-sprint BASE: v1.3/comms KIND: feature PRIORITY: blocker STOP: nova-sprint check cards reports each stream's critical-path length against its open cards and the waiting cards held only by overlap needs or soft dependencies, and warns, naming the stream or the edge, when a stream's critical path is more than half its ope Source: Glenn ~15:02Z 2026-10-15: \"How can we remember and enforce not putting toooooo restrictive dependencies on cards in future? I love the rigor, but we don't really need things running fully serial like this.\" At 14:50Z that day 269 cards were waiting on 466 need edges; one card was the only unlanded need of 115 others, and the schema streams ran a critical path of 15 of 18 and 17 of 25 open cards. Work audited 2026-10-15. No pushed head. "
   :why "Scoped out of the sprint by Glenn 2026-10-15: only the four tiny fixes stay in v13-blockers, tool-review-2026-10-15 and nova-local; the rest waits on the roadmap."
   :date "2026-10-15"
   :origin "sprint card check-warns-when-the-sprint-runs-serial (stream v13-blockers, column waiting, tier , base v1.3/comms), moved out of the sprint 2026-10-15"
