   :text "RESULT: prose-never-re-adds-a-need sha=<sha12> tier: frontier REPO: mas-bandwidth/nova-sprint BASE: v1.3/comms KIND: fix PRIORITY: critical STOP: a card's needs change only through its typed header's DEPENDS-ON: (or Needs:) line, needs set, a relink or a replace; no prose line, no stale waits_after record and no other field brings back a need the coordinator removed; the red tests named in DONE-WHEN pass at head, and Source: the needs audit of 2026-10-15 afternoon (working/tmp/needs-audit-2026-10-15-pm.md, \"A removed need comes back from prose\"): the morning's removal of go-table-writers-refuse-what-their-readers-refuse -> table-wire-over-text-transports came back after a later brief edit. That brief still carries the prose line `ORDER. DEPENDS-ON table-wire-over-text-transports (the schema-go chain); ...` below its header, and nine open schema-go briefs carry such a line. The owner's rule: needs are true dependenci Work audited 2026-10-15. No pushed head. "
   :why "Scoped out of the sprint by Glenn 2026-10-15: only the four tiny fixes stay in v13-blockers, tool-review-2026-10-15 and nova-local; the rest waits on the roadmap."
