  (item "adoption-is-measured" :group "export-v13-blockers" :area "nova-sprint"
   :title "adoption-is-measured"
   :text "RESULT: adoption-is-measured sha=<sha12> tier: heavy REPO: mas-bandwidth/nova-sprint BASE: v1.3/comms KIND: feature PRIORITY: blocker STREAM: v13-blockers STOP: `fleet beat` and a reader's `queue` take `--version <v>` and `--installed <v>` and keep both on the beat; `nova-sprint release adoption [<v>] [--json]` prints each release's live members and readers, how many report it installed and how many run it, and the a Source: the owner, 2026-10-15, verbatim: \"It should take no more than 5 minutes, and ideally just one minute to deploy a new release across our fleet.\" and \"make future releases meet the speed requirements.\" (The four-layer design, including the dashboard adoption tile, is the coordinator's, which the owner told to proceed.) The layer in full: the version travels in each member's beat; a release counts as adopted when every live member reports it, and an alarm (one judgment) fires if that has not happen Work audited 2026-10-15. No pushed head. "
   :why "Scoped out of the sprint by Glenn 2026-10-15: only the four tiny fixes stay in v13-blockers, tool-review-2026-10-15 and nova-local; the rest waits on the roadmap."
   :date "2026-10-15"
   :origin "sprint card adoption-is-measured (stream v13-blockers, column ready, tier , base v1.3/comms), moved out of the sprint 2026-10-15"
