   :kept (:sprint-card "adoption-is-measured" :sprint-stream "v13-blockers" :sprint-column "ready" :tier "" :sprint-base "v1.3/comms" :needs "" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch ""))
  (item "release-gates-are-card-receipts" :group "export-v13-blockers" :area "nova-sprint"
   :title "release-gates-are-card-receipts"
   :text "RESULT: release-gates-are-card-receipts sha=<sha12> tier: frontier REPO: mas-bandwidth/nova-sprint BASE: v1.3/comms KIND: feature PRIORITY: blocker STREAM: v13-blockers STOP: a primary whose brief's PATHS or NEW reach the sensitive list is dealt a security read beside its cold reads and leaves review only when it stands ok at the head; every card the land step lands gets a receipt, kept across clears and keyed by rep Source: The owner, 2026-10-15, approving four layers for the fast release pipeline, layer 2: the security read and the cold read happen per card at review and are recorded as receipts; at cut time the cut checks every commit since the last tag has its receipts, refuses naming the missing commit, and never runs a gate itself; per-release waivers stay possible and explicit. The v1.3.14 release read took 21 minutes at cut time. Work audited 2026-10-15. No pushed head. "
   :why "Scoped out of the sprint by Glenn 2026-10-15: only the four tiny fixes stay in v13-blockers, tool-review-2026-10-15 and nova-local; the rest waits on the roadmap."
