  (item "a-member-hold-releases-itself-at-its-time" :group "export-v15-features" :area "nova-sprint"
   :title "a-member-hold-releases-itself-at-its-time"
   :text "RESULT: a-member-hold-releases-itself-at-its-time sha=<sha12> tier: heavy REPO: mas-bandwidth/nova-sprint BASE: v1.5 KIND: feature PRIORITY: high STREAM: v15-features STOP: `nova-sprint hold <member>` takes exactly one of `--until <RFC3339>` or `--for <duration>`, or `--indefinite` with a `--reason`, and is refused naming the three when none is given; the control card keeps the release time; the tick releases an expi Source: the owner, 2026-10-15, verbatim: \"Please add a system for holding a machine, and then automatically releasing it at a future time or a time at some duration in the future from present. You can't remember to auto-release it. This has just been demonstrated.\" The demonstration: the coordinator held member amd-1 for a spike at 18:33Z, the spike ended, and the hold sat 49 minutes with nothing using the machine until the owner asked. The owner then placed this on v1.5, not v1.3. Work audited 2026-10-15. No pushed head. Working branch, not on origin: sprint/a-member-hold-releases-itself-at-its-time.w1.g2.e21 (emma, working when dropped). "
   :why "Scoped out of the sprint by Glenn 2026-10-15 (\"anything in v1.5 that is not related to schema adoption, move to v1.7\"): target v1.7."
   :date "2026-10-15"
   :release "v1.7"
   :origin "sprint card a-member-hold-releases-itself-at-its-time (stream v15-features, column working, tier , base v1.5), moved out of the sprint 2026-10-15"
